      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Schema Jisrael (Shema Yisrael)” is a hymn written by Moritz Mayer (1821-1867) and posthumously published in <tei:hi rend="italic">Hymns, for Divine Service in the Temple Emanu-El</tei:hi> (1871), hymn No33, pp. 66-67. It may have been published earlier in the author’s lifetime. From 1865-1867, Mayer would occassionally fill in for Rabbi Samuel Adler at Temple Emanu-El, as noted in the synagogues meeting minutes.<tei:anchor xml:id="note_1"/> If you know of an earlier source for this hymn, please leave a comment or contact us.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_51208_notes"/>
    </tei:front>
